# Day 27 - README and Favicon

## Learning Objectives

* Learned the purpose of a README file.
* Learned how to organize project information.
* Learned what a favicon is.
* Added a favicon to a webpage.

## README

A README is the introduction to a project. It explains what the project does, the technologies used, and how to run it.

## Favicon

A favicon is the small icon displayed in the browser tab.

Example:

```html
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="favicon.png">
```

## Practical Work

* Reviewed and improved my README.
* Added a favicon to my project.
* Verified the favicon appeared in the browser.

## Key Takeaways

* A good README helps others understand your project.
* A favicon makes a website look more professional.
